WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.187
Many ecommerce retailers refrain from investing in their return management process,

00:00:06.187 --> 00:00:08.113
and it’s hard to blame them.

00:00:08.113 --> 00:00:11.656
Returns can be expensive and time-consuming. 

00:00:11.656 --> 00:00:14.100
So here are 10 steps for retailers

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.729
to improve your returns management process,

00:00:16.729 --> 00:00:18.862
start reducing your returns,

00:00:18.862 --> 00:00:22.714
and profitably scale your ecommerce business.

00:00:22.714 --> 00:00:24.584
Let's get started.

00:00:29.819 --> 00:00:34.131
Number 1. Be Lenient with your Return Policies

00:00:34.131 --> 00:00:37.683
Your return policies impact your shopper conversion.

00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:41.174
If visitors don’t feel confident that they can return products,

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.380
they won’t feel confident in purchasing products.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:48.263
Number 2. Track as Much as You Can

00:00:48.263 --> 00:00:51.714
One missing button on a shirt seems minor, 

00:00:51.714 --> 00:00:55.410
but ten returns with missing buttons in two days

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.957
can pull an entire shipment of shirts off the shelf.

00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:03.103
Small observations help you discover big problems.

00:01:03.103 --> 00:01:08.680
Number 3. Prioritize People and Processes within Your Business

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.950
The people and processes within your organization

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.192
are every bit as important as the products you sell

00:01:15.192 --> 00:01:17.445
or the technology you use.

00:01:17.445 --> 00:01:20.942
Keep in mind that the most impactful observations

00:01:20.942 --> 00:01:24.264
often come from those who most frequently interact

00:01:24.264 --> 00:01:26.484
with products and shoppers.

00:01:26.484 --> 00:01:30.134
Number 4. Move Beyond a Spreadsheet

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:32.056
Spreadsheets are helpful

00:01:32.056 --> 00:01:36.564
but may not be ideal for advanced product and shopper analyses.  

00:01:36.564 --> 00:01:39.612
After sifting through endless rows of data,

00:01:39.612 --> 00:01:43.465
many retailers struggle to get information from insight.

00:01:43.465 --> 00:01:46.793
Leverage the power of return analytics software

00:01:46.793 --> 00:01:49.904
to aggregate customer feedback easily

00:01:49.904 --> 00:01:52.346
so you can get straight to the insights 

00:01:52.346 --> 00:01:55.119
and improve your return management process.

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:59.430
Number 5. Embrace Return Optimization

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:04.000
Return Optimization involves leveraging return data

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.560
to enhance the shopper experience,

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.130
improve operational efficiency, 

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.739
and grow your profits. 

00:02:11.739 --> 00:02:14.952
Accept that returns are a part of ecommerce.

00:02:14.952 --> 00:02:17.400
You will never eliminate returns,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.036
 but you can reduce returns and provide your shoppers 

00:02:21.036 --> 00:02:23.632
with a smooth return experience.  

00:02:23.632 --> 00:02:29.925
Number 6. Start with Basic Analyses, then Drill Deeper

00:02:29.925 --> 00:02:33.951
To collect real insights, we need more than data. 

00:02:33.951 --> 00:02:37.077
We need a logical flow of analyses.

00:02:37.077 --> 00:02:41.310
Return rates and reasons are an excellent place to start. 

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.896
They provide a quick summary of your product returns.

00:02:44.896 --> 00:02:48.607
Once you identify areas for potential improvement, 

00:02:48.607 --> 00:02:50.627
zoom into return comments

00:02:50.627 --> 00:02:52.627
and customer-level information

00:02:52.627 --> 00:02:55.690
to gather precise, contextual feedback.  

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.580
Number 7. Connect All Parts of Your Business

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:04.409
Returns are often not the responsibility of any single department.

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:09.511
They’re a natural and pervasive part of business in ecommerce, 

00:03:09.511 --> 00:03:13.269
so the best solutions require a holistic approach.

00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:15.860
A culture of collaboration – 

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.619
supported by mechanized communication – 

00:03:18.619 --> 00:03:21.297
can align the goals of different teams

00:03:21.297 --> 00:03:26.196
and produce better outcomes for both your shoppers and your business.

00:03:26.196 --> 00:03:30.348
Number 8. Act Upon Insights Immediately

00:03:30.348 --> 00:03:32.467
When you identify a problem,

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:36.474
try to find its cause as efficiently as possible.

00:03:36.474 --> 00:03:41.159
One apparel retailer confirmed that the quality of a particular fabric

00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:45.809
wasn’t as the factory had specified by looking at return comments.

00:03:45.809 --> 00:03:48.950
The team traced the faulty material to the products

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.247
and removed the SKU from their website

00:03:51.247 --> 00:03:54.526
before more shoppers could encounter the issue.

00:03:54.526 --> 00:04:00.122
Number 9. Transform Returns into an Opportunity for Loyalty

00:04:00.122 --> 00:04:04.158
As a retailer, you try to maximize the customer experience

00:04:04.158 --> 00:04:07.278
in all aspects of your ecommerce site.

00:04:07.278 --> 00:04:10.262
The return process should be no different.

00:04:10.262 --> 00:04:14.120
You can reimagine returns as a retention opportunity.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.744
The truth is, returns don’t have to cause churn, 

00:04:17.744 --> 00:04:21.766
and they don’t have to diminish your customer lifetime value.

00:04:21.766 --> 00:04:24.318
And lastly, Number 10

00:04:24.318 --> 00:04:28.264
Implement Software that Integrates with Existing Systems

00:04:28.264 --> 00:04:30.593
To make the most of its impact, 

00:04:30.593 --> 00:04:34.383
return management software needs to access data stores

00:04:34.383 --> 00:04:35.719
within your business.

00:04:35.719 --> 00:04:40.905
Make sure its API enables integration with your inventory management 

00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:43.669
and warehouse management software. 

00:04:43.669 --> 00:04:48.518
To find the answers to many of the most pervasive questions in ecommerce, 

00:04:48.518 --> 00:04:50.094
look at the data.

00:04:50.094 --> 00:04:52.002
Adopt these ten points, 

00:04:52.002 --> 00:04:55.391
and you’ll be well-positioned to take control of returns 

00:04:55.391 --> 00:05:00.010
and capitalize on insights that’ll drive your business forward. 

